note right of IImageSizeFacility
  Implemented by the consuming project.
  The library decodes no image format
  of its own.
end note

note bottom of IADataImportersFacade
  The only entry point a consuming
  project needs. Everything else stays
  behind these abstract interfaces.
end note

note bottom of Folder2DBImporter
  Everything an import does around the
  reading of its one layout: the guards,
  the image measuring, the merge into
  the database and the count.
end note

note bottom of JsonDescriptor2DBImporter
  What the two layouts described by a
  single JSON document share: locating
  that document among the files such a
  dataset may arrive with.
end note

note bottom of UltralyticsFolder2DBImporter
  The three Ultralytics YOLO layouts
  differ in one label file line only,
  which is the one thing the base
  leaves to its descendants.
end note

note bottom of IJsonParser
  The library links no JSON or XML
  library of its own. Neither reader
  knows anything of the layouts read
  through it.
end note

note bottom of OpenCVImageSizer
  Compiled only into a build which found
  OpenCV. A reader the consumer sets
  always wins over it.
end note

